WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.580
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.090
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.800
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.720
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.350
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.470
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.800
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.290
Come on!

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.820
Since you always end up buying this…

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.310
…there’s no reason to be indecisive.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.100
Come on, there’s a line behind you.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:19.580
Come on, let’s go!

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:02.270
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.840
and the listed sponsors.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.790
Really?!

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.760
Here!

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.270
Thanks.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.260
Shinohara-san!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.760
This…

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.790
It’s your big brother, right?

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:44.510
See?! I told you!

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:45.540
I can’t believe it!

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.090
It’s true!

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.280
The awaited new star: DJ Michi!

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.350
Real name: Shinohara Michi, 18 years old!

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.220
Amazing being in a book!

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.860
Your big brother also released a CD, right?

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.920
But it has other people’s songs…

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:03.890
And…

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.070
…it’s not mainstream.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.140
Indies, right?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.330
I’m jealous!

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.360
Hey, is your brother in Tokyo?

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.210
Does he ever come back here?

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:14.880
Occasionally.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.750
Get his signature next time!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.920
Yeah! I want one too!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.270
It’s OK, right?

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:21.900
Right?

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.530
Really!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.290
Don’t be so unreasonable!

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.160
What?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.400
We’re asking Shinohara-san!

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.400
Anyway, no!

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.390
Here!

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.190
Wasn’t Usagi’s big brother amazing?

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.240
Good grades, an amazing athlete…

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.640
I know!

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.010
He got a ton of Valentine’s chocolate too!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.870
The Chocolate Champion of Saigawara High School!

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.260
Compared to that…

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.700
It’ll go cold if we leave it up to you!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.550
I’ll do it for you, so wait.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.440
Thanks.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.530
Really, she gives us a lot of trouble.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.780
But she’s our friend since preschool.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:27.590
We’ve looked after her all this time.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.830
We can’t abandon her now.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.670
At least be a bit grateful, Usagi.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.760
Grateful…

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:04.800
I’m home!

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.600
Welcome home, Usagi.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.460
Welcome home.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.580
Big brother, you’ve returned!

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:18.260
He said he had some work close by.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.780
A concert, right?

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.120
An event.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.220
Events and concerts are different?

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.270
Silly father.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:31.770
Usagi, your big brother might be in an
 entertainment production.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.660
Really?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.810
I said I’ve only met an agent.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.460
Even that is impressive,

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.480
right?

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.370
Yes, I’m relieved things seem to be going smoothly.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.490
When he said he wasn’t going to college

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.040
and said he would follow the path of music…

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.570
I was worried what would happen, but…

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.090
Michito is reliable.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.720
So I thought he would do fine in any world. {as in, world of profession}

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.510
Since Michito is here, perfect timing.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.920
Usagi, it’s about what job you’ll do…

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:05.870
What?

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.590
Before this week was over, you promised us

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:12.200
to figure out what you were doing, remember?

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:13.910
How is it?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.790
Is there something you would like to do?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:16.580
What?

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.360
Were you not able to pick after all?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.090
We thought it would be like that.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.390
So I spoke with your father too, but…

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.820
Usagi, you’re nice.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.660
So wouldn’t nursing suit you?

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:42.070
I was thinking of consulting an acquaintance for you,

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:42.950
but what do you think?

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:50.940
Sure!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.350
Really? I’m glad!

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:57.430
Yes, I should get right to contacting him.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:07:59.860
Thanks.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.720
I’m going home.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.450
Oh?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.390
Later.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:12.900
Big brother!

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.780
Uh… um…

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.840
My friends wanted you to sign-

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:19.670
Are you really…

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.860
…OK with exactly what our old man and old lady said?

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:30.290
Whatever.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.620
You tortoise!

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.510
<i>Hey,</i>

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.700
<i>isn’t that your little sister?</i>

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.930
<i>I dunno.</i>

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.670
<i>Japanese…</i>

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:56.660
<i>Math…</i>

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.560
<i>And… what else was there?</i>

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:06.760
<i>Michito!</i>

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.340
<i>Go with Usagi to school!</i>

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:12.190
<i>I don’t want to! She’s slow!</i>

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.370
<i>I’m leaving!</i>

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.770
<i>Ah, Michito!</i>

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:15.940
<i>Science…</i>

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.350
<i>Planner…</i>

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:25.450
<i>Usagi will become big brother’s wife when I’m older!</i>

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:30.860
<i>Who would with you? You tortoise!</i>

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.010
Yuzuki!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:52.160
We’re going to study in the library, but…

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:53.800
If you’d like to…

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:57.300
Sorry, I have somewhere to go!

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.020
Hey!

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:15.240
Yes?

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:18.150
Um…

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.790
Hell Correspondence…!

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:21.710
Do you know what it is?

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.010
What?

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:27.330
Please don’t access the Hell Correspondence.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.240
No matter how much you begrudge them, hate them…

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.760
That can’t resolve anything!

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:34.980
Um…

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.760
Hell… What?

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.210
Hell Coresspondence…

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.490
You don’t know what it is?

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.490
I’m terribly sorry!

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:55.550
Uh… um…

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:00.750
What?!

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.040
Usagi got a boyfriend?! Who is he?!

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:05.730
Endo-kun, from our class!

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.250
Endo?

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.420
Oh! That dark one!

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:15.060
She said she was going to go home with him today.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:17.540
Wow, with that Usagi.

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:22.030
Since you guys don’t have boyfriends,

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.970
you got passed by that tortoise!

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.190
Me?

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.430
Yes.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:36.210
Can you be my part-time chief?

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:39.200
You’ve worked the longest among the current workers,

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.030
and Shinohara-kun you’re reliable.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.040
So, it’ll be a big help if you do accept.

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.540
But I’ve got music.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.500
You’re still doing that?

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.670
Since you’ve been coming daily recently,

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.330
I thought you quit.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.930
Well, think about it.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:05.350
Yes?

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:06.500
Hello?

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.020
Mother-

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.050
Listen, listen!

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:08.880
I’m busy right now, so-

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:12.100
Your mother was surprised, but-

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:12.100
What?

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.870
Usagi got a boyfriend!

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:20.630
Her life goals are set, and she got a match…

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:21.590
Really…

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:26.140
I was worried about that girl, so your mother was so glad!

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:43.930
Hey, Waro-waro!

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.310
Wind my spring!

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:47.480
Wait a bit longer, hime!

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:50.180
Faster! Faster!

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.400
I’m still helping Wanyudo-san.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.400
It’s fine, Waro-waro. She’s so loud I can’t help it.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.400
Come! Come quickly!

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:54.730
Y-Yes!

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:56.570
Come! You’re late!

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.400
Waro-waro, come!

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.400
She’ll be just as annoying if she could move.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:01.260
It’s still better if she goes away.

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.550
Wee!

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:04.670
Why does Ai only get a new body?

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:06.580
Kikuri wants one too!

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.200
Bang! Zip! Boom!

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.280
Bang? Zip?

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.480
She’s plenty “Boom!” as it is.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:13.420
Her head, that is.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:14.920
Ichimoku Ren-san.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:14.920
What did you say?

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:15.770
You eyeball!

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.930
By the way, how is it over there?

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:22.320
There seems to be no worry about her pulling the string.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.600
It’s cooked.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.100
Potatoes?

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.570
Thank you for the food. {Itadakimasu, which really means more than "Let’s Eat!" for example}

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:52.830
I’m jealous, Shinohara-san.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:54.330
Yes?

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.090
I feel relaxed when we’re together.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:05.090
Well…

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:07.860
Y-Yeah.

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:10.180
Later!

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.410
Where’s Usagi?

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:29.390
She said she’d drop by his house because
 she couldn’t contact him.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:32.240
Since he’s been absent for a while.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:33.850
Serves her right!

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:36.540
Even as a tortoise…

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.460
…passing us.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.980
Yeah, even though she’s a tortoise…

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:45.470
Grabbing at men… A perverted tortoise!

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:26.230
Thanks for coming for me.

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.130
Oh, the pizza will get cold.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.950
Your brother came to me…

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.690
…saying he had something to say about you.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.090
Since there was an event launch,

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.660
he invited me to go with him.

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:44.690
And…

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.530
...sorry.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.200
I don’t have a right to be with you.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.970
What do you want? Asking me to come so suddenly.

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:16.550
Um… yeah… well…

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.640
It’s about Endo-kun, but…

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:19.550
Oh?

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.550
You got the pictures?

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:23.520
Yeah.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:27.350
I thought it would be good to tell you.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.130
He’s that type of guy.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.950
I think it’ll be better if you broke up with him soon.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:34.810
Yes, we’ve already broken up.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:35.540
What?

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.020
We broke up accidentally.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.390
Usagi…

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:52.910
Here!

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.340
Stop!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.110
Stop!

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.110
You…!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.030
Is that… yours?

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:26.130
Were you going to send me?

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.970
Why do you hate me that much?

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:36.330
Because I’m good for nothing? Because I’m a tortoise?

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:37.660
Hey, big brother-!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.640
I was always jealous of you!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:43.020
I was always jealous of you.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.750
Our old man and old lady…

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.540
…were only worried about you since our childhood.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.730
Since I’m reliable,

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:53.950
I was always left alone.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.120
Because you can,

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.980
I couldn’t do anything.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.310
That’s why…

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.510
Go out to the city.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.200
Guys who can do more than me…

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.390
…are all over the place!

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.000
I was lying about my work going well!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.070
But you were in a book, and a CD…

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.020
You even said you were going to be in an entertainment production!

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.970
Our old man and old lady just conveniently misunderstood.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:21.510
That day, I was going to say I was quitting music.

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.270
That’s why I went home.

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:26.230
Hating being a good kid…

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:28.220
Running away from home and working part-time…

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.100
But…

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:32.210
Why do you become more fortunate than me?!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.910
Not working hard at all!

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:35.740
You only laughing so foolishly!

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.850
Why?! Why is it?!

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:46.630
I’m not fortunate at all. I know…

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:50.420
…my friends are really making fun of me.

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:55.430
Mom and Dad have completely given up on me.

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.370
I’m working hard too.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.900
But I can’t, I’m a tortoise.

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.170
Something like that…

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.690
Without laughing, it’s impossible to bear!

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.120
Let’s end this.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:17.450
Doing this as siblings… Let’s end this.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.460
Big brother!

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.130
Usagi.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:47.320
I did something horrible to your boyfriend.

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:50.060
But, well…

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.820
You’ll find another good guy.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:56.160
Not just a boyfriend…

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.250
Don’t give up!

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:00.920
If you work hard there are things even you can do.

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:03.030
Even you.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.100
Wh-What is this?!

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:32.100
Whoa!

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.010
Oh, shit!

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.290
Someone help me!

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:38.200
Tortoise, tortoise, tortoise, tortoise, tortoise, tortoise, tortoise!

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.670
What? It can’t be!

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:09.550
Why?

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.810
Your little sister pulled the string.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.800
Usagi did?

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:16.690
That’s a lie.

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.610
We said we’d get along from now on.

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:20.330
Lies!

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.770
Says he, Ojou.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.600
O pitiful shadow, wandering in darkness.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.080
Scarring people and looking down on them.

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:34.930
The ball of karma is drowned in sin.

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:41.810
Would you like to die this once?

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:44.910
Loincloth booster!

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.150
Why…

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.530
Even I can do it.

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:03.730
Even I…

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:05.660
Even I…

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:07.660
Even I!

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:12.670
<i>Usagi will become big brother’s wife when I’m older!</i>

00:22:13.090 --> 00:22:15.870
<i>Who would with you? You tortoise!</i>

00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:27.810
If you become beautiful… I’ll marry you.

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:49.820
Note: Candle says,  Shinohara Usagi.

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:49.820
Your hatred I shall release.

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:22.860
Your name?

00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:23.800
Nawa Akihiro.

00:24:24.580 --> 00:24:28.260
Did you ferry that man to Hell?

00:24:28.630 --> 00:24:31.160
I rescued Kae-chan.

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:34.610
If I had let her be, he would have… Kae-chan… {there’s no verb, but you need the object (Kae-chan) in there…}

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:36.520
I don’t regret it.

00:24:37.520 --> 00:24:39.960
I will live tightly carrying that sin.

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:44.440
But this isn’t the end necessarily.

00:24:45.100 --> 00:24:48.030
Next time: The Alluring Trap.

